e adjustments.␀␀␀␀This is useful for getting the exact shot that you want.␀␀␀␀Hold down the right mouse button to speed up time.␀␀This is helpful when waiting for moving objects.␀␀␀␀Click the left mouse button to fire the ball.␀␀␀The ball will head right to where your mouse was when you clicked.␀␀Move your mouse cursor to where you want the ball to go.␀␀␀␀The Launcher will automatically aim so that the ball heads to that point.␀␀␀The green peg activates your Magic Power.␀␀␀There are two green pegs per level.␀The purple peg is worth 50x the value of the blue pegs.␀This peg changes location on every shot.␀␀␀␀Orange pegs are worth 10x the value of blue pegs.␀␀␀Clear all of the orange pegs on a level to beat the level.␀␀Pegs can be both round and rectangular.␀There are four types of pegs in Peggle.␀After beating a level you earn extra points from the bonus holes.␀␀␀You also earn 10,000 points per extra ball left over.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Certain cool shots give you extra style points.  These points add directly␀␀␀␀␀␀to your score and don't factor into getting a 25,000 point Free Ball.␀␀␀The value of the pegs goes up as you eliminate orange pegs.␀␀␀␀␀The Fevermeter on the right shows the current score multiplier.␀Every peg that you hit on a shot adds to a subtotal score.␀␀␀␀␀␀The shot score is the subtotal score multiplied by the number of pegs hit.␀␀␀␀␀␀The number of points you get for a shot is the total value of all of the pegs␀␀␀multiplied by the number of pegs you hit.␀␀␀In Duel Mode, you get style points instead of Free Balls.␀␀␀Also, there are no coin flip Free Balls in Duel Mode.␀␀␀If you don't hit any pegs on a shot then you may be awarded␀a Free Ball by winning a coin flip!␀Scoring 25K, 75K, and 125K on a shot also gives you a Free Ball.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀You get a Free Ball if your ball lands in the Free Ball Bucket.␀There are a few different ways to get a Free Ball.␀␀Challenge Mode presents you with extra difficult Peggle feats.␀␀Beat all of the challenges to become a Peggle Grand Master.␀Duel Mode allows you to compete in a two player version of Peggle.␀␀You can play against the computer or another person.␀␀␀␀Quick Play Mode lets you select an individual level to play.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀You may only play levels that you've completed in Adventure Mode.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Adventure Mode allows you to train with all the Peggle Masters.␀Progress through all the levels to become a Peggle Master yourself.␀There are four game modes in Peggle.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀The game ends either when a player eliminates the last orange peg or␀␀␀␀when both players run out of balls.␀You must hit at least one orange peg on a shot.␀␀␀␀␀If you don't then you are penalized by losing 25% of your total score.␀␀In Duel Mode, two players take turns shooting the ball.␀The player with the most points at the end of the game wins.␀␀␀␀Duel Mode has slightly different rules than the single player modes.␀␀␀␀You can save replays and view them later!␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Click the Replays button on the main menu to view saved replays.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Hold down the left mouse button in the play area to activate slow motion.␀␀␀Hold down the right button to activate fast forward.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Right click the Instant Replay button to enable an advanced mode in which␀␀␀you can replay all shots for a game.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Click the Instant Replay button on the bottom right of the game to␀␀see a replay of the last shot.␀␀␀␀␀␀Instant replays are useful for reliving your favorite shots and showing them␀␀␀␀to your friends and family over and over again.␀Click the Open Folder button in the Show Replays dialog to locate replays.␀␀␀␀␀␀Send replays to friends from here, or drop friends' replays in here to view.␀␀␀␀It's rumored that there's a level of Peggle Mastery beyond Grand Master.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Supposedly, clearing every level can help you attain this rank!␀Clearing all of the pegs on a level gives you a bonus blue ribbon!␀␀␀␀␀␀After beating Adventure Mode, you can replay it again using any Peggle␀␀Master on any level!  Can you top your high score?␀␀What else, what else, 